  "rationale": "The preseason finale comes down to four-quarter execution at Nissan Stadium, with uncertain starter workloads making the reserve phases especially important.\n\nTennessee’s latest game provides the stronger verified four-quarter performance. The Titans recovered from a 16-3 deficit, scored the final 16 points and beat Seattle 19-16. Chicago’s latest full rotation allowed Cincinnati’s backup offense to sustain a 14-play, 67-yard opening drive and later produce two second-quarter touchdown passes in a 27-9 Bears loss.\n\nTennessee’s comeback was not clean—it benefited from a muffed punt and a missed 44-yard field goal—and its offense with Cam Ward produced only one touchdown across six reported preseason possessions. Those concerns make laying 1.5 less attractive. At only a 10-cent difference from Tennessee -1.5 at -110, I would rather pay -120 on the moneyline and remove the risk of a one-point Titans victory.\n\nThis is a modest-confidence position based on Tennessee having shown the more credible recent path to finishing a full preseason game, not on assuming its starters control all four quarters.",
